meta {
  name: Send Notification
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/notifications/send?useQueue=true
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  useQueue: true
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": "user123",
    "userType": "customer",
    "notificationTypeCode": "order_created",
    "channel": "email",
    "recipient": "customer@example.com",
    "variables": {
      "orderNumber": "ORD-12345",
      "customerName": "John Doe",
      "orderTotal": "$99.99"
    },
    "metadata": {
      "orderId": "order-uuid-123",
      "source": "api"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Send Notification
  
  Sends a notification through the specified channel.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `userId` | string | **Required** | User ID |
  | `userType` | string | **Required** | User type (customer, driver, admin) |
  | `notificationTypeCode` | string | **Required** | Notification type code |
  | `channel` | string/array | Optional | Channel code(s) (email, sms, push, web). If omitted, resolves all active channels for the notification type. |
  | `recipient` | string | Optional | Recipient address (email, phone, device token, etc.) |
  | `variables` | object | Optional | Variables for template rendering |
  | `metadata` | object | Optional | Additional metadata |
  
  ## Flow
  1. Validates notification type exists and is active
  2. Checks user preferences (blocks if disabled)
  3. Finds appropriate template
  4. Validates required variables
  5. Renders template with variables
  6. Sends through channel handler
  7. Logs delivery attempt
  
  ## Example Response
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "code": 200,
    "message": "Notification sent successfully",
    "data": {
      "notificationId": "uuid",
      "status": "SENT",
      "channel": "email",
      "recipient": "customer@example.com",
      "messageId": "email-1234567890"
    }
  }
  ```
}
